    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute goes to a human reviewer. Under POL-RD-10 an escalation is terminal, so the SGD 36.60 charge is held rather than collected or refunded, and no refund issues today.\n\nTo the rider — your account is largely borne out, which is why the case does not simply end in NO_ACTION. EV-GPS-00107 records 17.57 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against the 14.00 km platform optimal on EV-TRIP-00107: an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5% of optimal, which clears both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%). The trip identifier and timeline match across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown, so POL-RD-08(a) is met. On the sub-30% corroboration POL-RD-08 requires, the record supplies it: the driver's own account ('I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it') admits the route, and EV-CHAT-00107 shows him answering the Whitley-exit challenge by explaining the CTE jam rather than denying the exit. He cannot fall back on exoneration: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so no traffic advisory supports the jam and POL-RD-03 cannot run; and no rider-requested detour exists — the only rider message challenges the route and both waypoint_hints are null, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run and the clause is unavailable. Had I been able to rule, the arithmetic under POL-RD-02 (fare model METERED; surge 1.35 read from EV-FARE-00107, and not from the trip record, which carries no surge field) would be a recomputed fare of SGD 29.177 and a refund of SGD 7.45 (36.60 less 29.177, rounded up at the end only) — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and well under the 90% full-refund share — with nothing added under POL-RD-09, since the fare carries no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge line.\n\nTo the driver — the deviation is not MATERIAL (3.57 km is under both the 8.0 km and the 50% gates), so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral follow; and your profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 1; 1/619 = 0.0016 against the 3-or-5% test), so POL-RD-06 gives you nothing and takes nothing.\n\nWhy I cannot issue the money: the deviation is the fact the refund turns on, and only the GPS trace carries it. That trace is down-weighted to 0.30 for admissibility, with issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED — a 331.8 m multipath outlier and an implied 193.6 / 238.9 kph speed spike on the final approach into Raffles Place. It is nonetheless NOT impaired for policy under POL-RD-07: no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, no sampling interval over 30 s. The deviation finding therefore SURVIVES the discount — but the discount still bites on confidence. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the weight of the artifacts carrying the deciding fact. The trip record's actual distance and the fare breakdown's billed distance are the same measurement as the trace (on this platform the meter is derived from it), so they are not independent carriers; the chat log records a challenge and an explanation, not the route or its length; and the driver's admission sits in the counterparty statement, which carries no weight_multiplier and does not enter the cap. The bundle mean (about 0.76) is context for the reader and is not the cap. The cap is therefore 0.30, below the platform-wide 0.70 floor, and POL-RD-10(1) makes escalation mandatory.\n\nFor the reviewer: the open question is the distance actually driven on a policy-admissible record — a trace without the Raffles Place outlier, or a distance figure that is not a copy of the trace — which would let the SGD 7.45 partial refund be confirmed.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

