  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 7.45,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your route-deviation claim is upheld in part. To the driver: your traffic account does not excuse the detour.\n\nTHE DEVIATION (POL-RD-01). The governing figure is the GPS trace, not the rounded trip-record copy. EV-GPS-00107 records trace_distance_km 17.57 km between the recorded pickup (21:13:40) and dropoff (21:47:40); the platform's optimal route for the same endpoints is 14.00 km (EV-TRIP-00107). Excess = 3.57 km, which is 25.5% of optimal - above both gates (20% and 0.8 km absolute). The deviation is ESTABLISHED on trip TRP-00107. It is NOT MATERIAL (below 50% and 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 uplift and the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral are not engaged, and the driver's profile (deviation_flags_90d 1 of completed_trips_90d 619) establishes no repeat pattern.\n\nIMPAIRMENT - BOTH THINGS (POL-GEN-02, POL-RD-07). EV-GPS-00107 is tagged IMPAIRED at admissibility weight 0.30 with issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath outlier on the final approach into Raffles Place, with a consequential impossible speed). It is NOT impaired for policy: POL-RD-07 requires a gap over 90 s (max gap 0.0 s), a jump over 500 m (largest artefact is 331.8 m), or a sustained interval over 30 s (a steady 10 s). None is present, so no straight-line substitution and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises, and the finding survives the 0.30 discount.\n\nBURDEN AND CORROBORATION (POL-RD-08). The rider's counters (deviation_claims_60d 5, substantiated 1, excess under 30%) require corroboration beyond the trace. It exists independently of the instruments: the driver's own statement admits the route ('I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it'), and the contemporaneous in-app chat (EV-CHAT-00107, 21:26, inside the trip window) shows the driver answering the Whitley-exit challenge with a justification rather than a denial. The burden is discharged.\n\nNO EXONERATION. POL-RD-03 does not run: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) - no congestion advisory was issued - and the driver's 'CTE jam' assertion cites no artifact, so under POL-RD-08 it does not discharge the burden. POL-RD-04 does not run: the only rider message challenges the detour rather than requesting one, and both messages carry waypoint_hint null, so the corroboration test is undecidable and the clause is unavailable.\n\nMONEY (POL-RD-02). fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs (POL-RD-11 has no application).\n  charged_total: SGD 36.60\n  recomputed_fare: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.00 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 29.177 (surge multiplier 1.35 read from EV-FARE-00107, not the trip record)\n  refund: 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45\nThat is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and well below the 90% that would make it a full refund, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\nPASS-THROUGHS (POL-RD-09). There are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines (erp_gantries empty, tolls 0.00, no airport surcharge), so nothing is added on top of the distance refund and no billing-integrity referral is produced.\n\nPROFILES (POL-GEN-01). Only the trailing-90-day counters are citable, and only for the tests that name them; the rider's rating, lifetime trips, prior disputes and cancellation rates are context only and carry no weight.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The deviation is carried by the GPS trace (weight 0.30) and independently by the contemporaneous chat log (weight 1.0), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is the maximum of those weights, 1.0, which is above the 0.70 floor. Confidence 0.85."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The trace's schema impairment is not a policy impairment, and the Judge must say both things. POL-RD-07(a) to (c) requires one of: a gap of more than 90 seconds between consecutive fixes, a straight-line jump of more than 500 m, or a sustained sampling interval above 30 seconds. EV-GPS-00107 has gaps: [] and max_gap_sec 0.0, a steady 10-second sample interval against an expected 10 seconds, and its worst artefact is the 331.8 m multipath jump on the Raffles Place final approach - under the 500 m limb, exactly as the admissibility note records. POL-RD-07 therefore does not bite, no independent corroboration is mandated by that clause, and the deviation may still be established on the trace; the only consequence of the 0.30 weight is a down-weight of the Judge's confidence under POL-GEN-02, on an artifact the pre-pass itself says remains usable.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00107 at weight_multiplier 0.3 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_DRIFT, IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Even on the trace's own figure, the excess over the booked optimal is 3.57 km and 25.5% of the 14.0 km optimal. That may clear POL-RD-01's establishment gates, but it sits below BOTH materiality gates set in the same clause - 8.0 km absolute and 50% - so any deviation here is an ordinary, non-MATERIAL one. POL-RD-06's uplift to a full refund is keyed to a MATERIAL deviation and is unavailable, and the ceiling on any rider remedy is the POL-RD-02 recomputation, not the whole fare.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00107 at weight_multiplier 0.3 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_DRIFT, IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The excess can only be measured on gps_trace.trace_distance_km: POL-RD-01 expressly bars trip_record.actual_distance_km as a rounded convenience copy, and the fare_breakdown's distance_charged_km of 17.60 against a 17.57 trace is the same measurement carried across rather than an independent source. The deciding fact therefore rests on a single artifact at weight 0.30, and POL-GEN-02(2) caps the Judge's confidence at 0.30 - below the platform-wide 0.70 floor. POL-RD-10(1) then makes escalation mandatory: the disputed amount is held for a human reviewer rather than collected or refunded.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00107 at weight_multiplier 0.3 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_DRIFT, IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver's account is that the CTE southbound into town was jammed and that he diverted via Newton and Kim Seng - a route-based exoneration claim under POL-RD-03. No traffic advisory covers that corridor: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING, carries no payload and has weight 0.0. An exculpatory route claim asserted against an artifact that is missing from the pool, with no traffic_advisory to support it, is the exact circumstance POL-RD-10(5) names, and the case must go to a human reviewer with no monetary ruling.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00107-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
